# BrewPhoria root .gitignore — defense-in-depth on top of backend/.gitignore and
# mobile/.gitignore. Keeps credentials and heavy design exports out of the repo.

# Design export assets (Claude Design HTML/CSS/image export — reference material,
# not part of the shipped app; ~28MB, kept out of git to keep clones small)
/BrewPhoria Mobile Redesign/

# Internal / local-only docs — kept on disk, not in the public repo.
/RECOMMENDATIONS.md
/CONTEXT.md
/DEMO_MODE.md

# Local tooling config
**/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Stray artifacts
/package-lock.json
**/shot.png

# Claude Code local tooling/session config (launch.json, skills) — machine-local,
# not part of the app. No leading slash so it's caught at any depth (root and
# mobile/.claude/ both).
.claude/

# Environment / secrets (defense in depth — also covered per-package)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties

# Service-account / admin credentials — must never be committed
**/private_key.json
**/serviceAccount*.json
**/firebase-adminsdk*.json

# Native Firebase config (contains per-platform client keys) — regenerate locally
# via `flutterfire configure` / the Firebase console rather than committing.
# Flutter's own generated `firebase_options.dart` IS safe to commit (Firebase's own
# guidance) and is intentionally NOT excluded here.
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
**/google-services.json

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
